# Dual remotes (GitHub + Azure)

Every push must update **both** remotes:

1. `origin` → GitHub SSH: `git@github.com:ahmadubuntu/gnome-cisco-vpn.git`
2. `azure` → `https://azure.charisma.tech/DataPlatform/DataPlatform/_git/gnome-cisco-vpn`

Do **not** put Azure on `origin` pushurl (Azure needs PAT header; mixed pushurls fail the Azure leg after GitHub succeeds).

## Auth

Use **`AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM`** (never `AZDO_PAT`).

```bash
AUTH_HEADER="AUTHORIZATION: Basic $(printf ':%s' "$AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM" | base64 -w0)"
git push origin HEAD
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure HEAD
# when tags changed:
git push origin --tags
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure --tags
```

Rules:
- Never print/commit the PAT; never put it in `git remote set-url`
- Encode empty username: `:PAT` (colon + token)
- Keep branch upstream on `origin/<branch>` (GitHub), not `azure/*`
- Do not commit `schemas/gschemas.compiled`
